  "status": "Refused",
  "description": "We propose a single-storey 4500 mm rear extension. The side extension will be 75 mm, aligned with our main building line; however, the minimum setback from the boundary must be 1100 mm. An L-shaped rear-to-side dormer will replicate the one on the neighbouring property.\nWe will maintain the current ridge height. Additionally, we will ensure a minimum 300 mm setback from the existing ridge to the new flat roof over the loft space. Rooflights will be installed on the front and side roof slopes. External alterations include the demolition of the existing rear bay window and both side and rear dormers.",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:12.0pt;line-height:115%;\r\nfont-family:&amp;quot;Aptos&amp;quot;,sans-serif;mso-ascii-theme-font:minor-latin;mso-fareast-font-family:\r\nAptos;mso-fareast-theme-font:minor-latin;mso-hansi-theme-font:minor-latin;\r\nmso-bidi-font-family:&amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;;mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi;\r\nmso-ansi-language:EN-GB;mso-fareast-language:EN-US;mso-bidi-language:AR-SA&quot;&gt;The proposed single storey rear extension by reason of its projection and\r\nproximity to the shared boundary with No.70 Wellington Road, would result in an\r\nobtrusive and overbearing form of development resulting in an unacceptable\r\nsense of enclosure and loss of outlook for the residents of No.70 Wellington Road,&amp;nbsp;contrary to the high\r\nquality design aspirations of the National Planning Policy Framework (2024),\r\nPolicy D3 of The London Plan (2021), Core Policy CS1.B of the Harrow Core\r\nStrategy (2012), Policy DM1 of the Harrow Development Management Policies Local\r\nPlan (2013) and the adopted Supplementary Planning Document: Residential Design\r\nGuide (2010).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;"
  ],
